[[0,1608137,0,2,0,2,"2017-02-01T07:28:07","TheBeautifulOne","",[],"","Boycotting Marvel Comics: What Are We Willing To Risk To Make A Point?","https://www.bleedingcool.com/2017/01/31/boycotting-marvel-comics-willing-risk-make-point/","Marvel"],[1,7846044,0,1,0,1,"2017-02-01T12:59:39","fricknmaniac","",[],"<p>Pretty much the only thing of value that came out of that article was the point that boycotting merchandise is more effective than boycotting comics. And the reason that's true is because comic book readers don't care about the writer's agenda, they care about good writing. Going after niche markets (like people who want a character to be a minority or people who don't want a character to be a minority) will never work because the comic book market isn't large enough for niche comics like that from major publishers (it can work from independent publishers because then it's more about the finished product than making money).</p>\n<p>We've consistently seeing that titles created for and written with an agenda get canceled quickly due to poor sales (Angela Queen of Hel and Mockingbird), but titles that focus on good writing first and have a minority character second (like Jane Foster Thor, Miles Morales Spider-man, or Kamala Khan Ms. Marvel) do really well in sales.</p>"]]
